; Several RenderWorld calls per frame against what the original Blitz3D 1.118 draws. In the original huge scenes had to be
; split over many RenderWorld calls (a surface holds at most 65535 vertices and 16383 sprites crash it), and the later
; calls kept the colors and depth of the earlier ones when CameraClsMode switched the clearing off. The expected pixels were
; recorded from the original (Direct3D 7 through Wine): run this program with MULTI_RECORD=1 in the environment to get them
; in record.txt and the pictures of every scene next to it. It covers the clear flags of CameraClsMode, depth and color that
; persist, sprites and transparent surfaces that test against what an earlier call drew, viewports and the order of several
; cameras, TrisRendered, one particle buffer that is sorted and updated between calls, and 50 calls per frame.
; Skipped without a window.
Include "check.bb"

If GetEnv$("BLITZ_HEADLESS") <> "" Then
	Print "blitz3d_multi_render_original_pixels: skipped, there is no window."
	End
EndIf

Graphics3D 160, 120, 32, 2
SetBuffer BackBuffer()

Const TOLERANCE = 6

Global record = (GetEnv$("MULTI_RECORD") <> "")
Global out
If record Then out = WriteFile("record.txt")

; Checks the pixel against what the original drew, or writes down what this one draws.
Function Px(name$, x, y, wr, wg, wb)
	c = ReadPixel(x, y, BackBuffer())
	r = (c Shr 16) And 255
	g = (c Shr 8) And 255
	b = c And 255
	If record Then
		WriteLine out, name$ + " " + r + " " + g + " " + b
	Else
		Check name$ + " red at " + x + "," + y, r, wr, TOLERANCE
		Check name$ + " green at " + x + "," + y, g, wg, TOLERANCE
		Check name$ + " blue at " + x + "," + y, b, wb, TOLERANCE
	EndIf
End Function

Function Shot(name$)
	If record Then SaveBuffer BackBuffer(), name$ + ".bmp"
End Function

; A number the program counts, with the one the original counted.
Function Note(name$, value, want)
	If record Then
		WriteLine out, name$ + " " + value
	Else
		Check name$, value, want, 0
	EndIf
End Function

; A flat quad facing the camera at the distance z, half the size of "half" in each direction, fullbright.
Function Quad(z#, half#, red, green, blue)
	m = CreateMesh()
	s = CreateSurface(m)
	AddVertex s, -1, -1, 0
	AddVertex s, -1, 1, 0
	AddVertex s, 1, 1, 0
	AddVertex s, 1, -1, 0
	AddTriangle s, 0, 1, 2
	AddTriangle s, 0, 2, 3
	ScaleEntity m, half, half, 1
	EntityColor m, red, green, blue
	EntityFX m, 1
	PositionEntity m, 0, 0, z
	Return m
End Function

Global cam = CreateCamera()
CameraRange cam, 0.1, 100

; Starts a scene: nothing is shown, the camera clears everything to the color.
Function Begin(red, green, blue)
	CameraClsMode cam, 1, 1
	CameraClsColor cam, red, green, blue
	CameraViewport cam, 0, 0, 160, 120
	RenderWorld
End Function

; The first call of a scene fills the picture with the color, so what comes after only has to show up on top of it.
Function Keep()
	CameraClsMode cam, 0, 0
End Function

; The screen is 160 x 120: at the distance z the camera sees z wide to both sides, and 0.75 z up and down, so 1 unit is
; 80 / z pixels at z. A quad of the size 3 at z = 10 covers x 56 to 104 and y 36 to 84.

